# Vali syscall definitions.
#
# Columns: number  wrapper name (without Syscall_)  kernel handler  return cast  arguments
# Arguments are comma-separated C identifiers. Use - for no arguments (maximum five).
# Names and return casts describe the libc macro; kernel prototypes remain in entry.c.
# Numbers are ABI values: keep existing numbers and append new calls at the end.
# All numbers from zero through the last entry must be present. Row order is ignored.
# Comments start with #. Python 3 and its standard library are sufficient.
#
# Regenerate: python3 tools/generate_syscalls.py
# Verify:     python3 tools/generate_syscalls.py --check

# Operating System (Module) Interface
0      Debug                                ScSystemDebug                          oserr_t   _level, _msg
1      MigrateLogs                          ScMigrateKernelLog                     oserr_t   _buffer, _size, _readOut
2      MapBootFramebuffer                   ScMapBootFramebuffer                   oserr_t   BufferOut
3      MapRamdisk                           ScMapRamdisk                           oserr_t   BufferOut, LengthOut
4      CapabilityGrant                      ScCapabilityGrant                      oserr_t   _capability, _handle

